  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRD in Kosovo 2016-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CRD in Kosovo 2016-2018</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CRD har presenterat ett f&#xf6;rslag som inneb&#xe4;r ett &#xe5;rs forts&#xe4;ttning av projektet &#x201d;Improving Access to Information and Equality in Kosovo 2016-2018&#x201d;. Det totala st&#xf6;det f&#xf6;r perioden 2016-2018 uppg&#xe5;r till 14 715 000 SEK.

Efter en analys av den &#xf6;vergripande situationen och med tanke p&#xe5; omst&#xe4;ndigheterna kommer Sida att f&#xf6;rbereda ett kompletterande beslut f&#xf6;r 1 &#xe5;r med utfasning och slutf&#xf6;rande av CRD:s bilaterala program i Kosovo.

Sida kommer att f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;nga samarbetsavtalet med CRD med ett &#xe5;r till 30 juni 2019 med en aktivitetsperiod till 31 december 2018.

CRD has presented a proposal to continue for eight months the project &quot;Improving Access to Information and Equality in Kosovo 2016-2018&quot;.  The total amount for support for the period 2016-2018 is 14 715 000 SEK.

CRD has submitted revised budget 2016-2108 and consequence analysis. After an analysis of the overall situation and considering the circumstances allocations, Sida has prepared a supplementary decision for a  phasing out and finalization of the CRD bilateral program in Kosovo adding 4.0 MSEK for 2018 covering the activity period to 31st  December 2018.
Sida will extend the cooperation agreement with CRD until 30 June 2019.

The following articles will be amended.
Article 2 - Activity period of the Project; Article 3 &#x2013; Financing of the project and provisional disbursement schedule;  Article 5  - Reporting &amp; Recovery; Article 7 &#x2013; Audit; Article 12 &#x2013; Termination.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Civil Rights Defenders in Kosovo 2016-2018</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRD&apos;s intervention is to strengthen the capacities of local CSOs to act as agents for change, furthering a more pluralistic civil society. CRD has developed solid partnerships with the overall objective to seek accountability of office-holders, furthering citizens&apos; demand for increased responsibility from the state. CRD supported free and independent media and it has been prioritised in the proposal through journalist&apos;s associations and alternative media channels. CRD works in increasing the respect for the human rights of vulnerable groups in Kosovo with specific focus on RAE communities hence combating discrimination. As this was phasing out period, Sida has assessed that there are no changes in relation to it previous assessment.</narrative>
  </description>
